@startuml flow-question-to-answer
' The central flow: a question arrives, joins a topic, gets an answer, reaches the room.
'
' Render:  plantuml docs/diagrams/flow-question-to-answer.puml

title Flow — from a question asked to an answer published

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #4A5568
  LifeLineBorderColor #7C86A0
  ParticipantBorderColor #7C86A0
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FDFDFD
}

actor Attendee
participant "Angular SPA" as SPA
participant "Spring Boot" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Kafka\n(questions.incoming)" as Kafka
participant "AI service\n(FastAPI)" as AI
actor Moderator

== Asking ==

Attendee -> SPA : types a question
SPA -> API : POST /api/questions/submit-question
activate API

API -> API : MeetingScope.activeMeetingId()
API -> DB : INSERT question (status=RECEIVED, meeting_id)\n**Durable record saved first**

alt HTTP mode (synchronous)
  API -> AI : POST /ingest\n{text, attendeeId, weight, meeting_id}
  activate AI
  AI -> AI : embed (384-dim) & find nearest centroid
  AI --> API : {cluster_id, size, is_new}
  deactivate AI
  API -> DB : UPDATE question SET cluster_id = resolved
  API --> SPA : {cluster_id, is_new} (attendee response)
  API -> AI : POST /draft (async via ClusterDraftWorker)\n**LLM answer pre-drafted on arrival**
else Kafka mode (event-sourced)
  API -> Kafka : publish to questions.incoming
  API --> SPA : {cluster_id: "pending"} (fast ack)
  Kafka -> AI : consume question event
  AI -> AI : embed & assign to cluster
  AI -> AI : auto-draft if cluster new / un-drafted
end

deactivate API
SPA --> Attendee : "question submitted"

== Ranking & Live Board ==

API -> AI : GET /clusters?meeting_id=…\n(after ingest or via BoardRefreshScheduler)
AI --> API : clusters ranked by log(1+size) × (1+weight) + draft
API -> SPA : STOMP push /topic/board (WebSocket)\nAngular signals re-render live

== Reviewing & Publishing Answer ==

alt Pre-drafted on arrival (default)
  Moderator -> SPA : views live board (grounded draft & citations ready)
else Manual draft request
  Moderator -> SPA : clicks "Draft answer"
  SPA -> API : POST /api/clusters/draft-answer
  API -> AI : POST /draft {cluster_id, question, meeting_id}
  AI --> API : {answer, citations}
  API -> DB : UPSERT cluster_draft (published = false)
  API --> SPA : draft + citations
end

Moderator -> SPA : edits, then publishes
SPA -> API : POST /api/room/publish-answer
API -> DB : cluster_draft.published = true
API -> SPA : push to every attendee board

SPA --> Attendee : the answer appears,\nwith the documents it came from

== If the AI service is down ==

SPA -> API : POST /api/chat/semantic-search
API -> AI : POST /search
AI --> API : ✗ connection refused
API --> SPA : **503** "The AI service is not available\nright now… try again shortly."
note over API
  Not a bare 500. Every AiClient call used
  to end in .block() with no handler and no
  logger, so an outage reached the SPA as
  Spring's default error page — no message
  to show, and no log line to diagnose it
  from. See AiClient.await().
end note

@enduml
